{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLUUXTMZU1LxDV7gZttP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `budget` loop is implemented. It posts one status-issue comment per capped scope (the repo or a role) per UTC day and records a `budget_capped` event. A restart does not repeat a notice, because the loop checks for that event first.\n\n`go build ./...`, `gofmt` and the tests for `internal/budget`, `internal/servecmd` and `internal/state` pass. I did not run `make lint` or the full `go test ./...`.\n\nThe comment follows the plan's template. It holds only numbers, the UTC day and config names. A role name that isn't `[a-z0-9._/-]+` is shown as `?`, so no `@` can get in. It also carries the estimate line and the steps for raising the cap. If posting fails, no event is written and the next tick retries. Under dry-run the comment goes through the same effects path.\n\nKnown gaps:\n- **Dry-run ledger test:** there is no `internal/servecmd` test that checks the comment lands in the real dry-run ledger file. Dry-run is covered only with a fake effects whose `DryRun()` returns true, and a negative issue number.\n- **Duplicate on crash:** a crash between posting the comment and recording the event can repeat one notice, as the plan accepted.\n\nI updated the loop-count and known-loops tests for the new loop, and `docs/proposal.md` in the Budgets, Observability and `--loops` text. The report is written to `.ard/237/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":805,"cache_read_input_tokens":49879,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":805},"output_tokens":473,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8e94895a-9c89-43aa-8887-d0